-- title:
--   Occurrence of the residual eigensystem in a corner at level Nr
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over $k$ (a representation of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ factoring through a finite level) which is absolutely irreducible, i.e. irreducible after base change to $\overline{k}$, and, viewed as an adic representation, ordinary at $p$: over each valuation subring lying over $p$ there is a rank-one direct summand stable under the decomposition group on which inertia acts through quotients landing in it. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes with $p\in S$, let $N\neq 0$ with $p\nmid N$ and all prime divisors of $N$ in $S$, and let $S_{\min}\subseteq S$ contain $p$ and satisfy: for primes $q\neq p$, $q\in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$; every $q\in S_{\min}$ with $q\neq p$ divides $N$; every prime $q\neq p$ dividing $N$ but not in $S_{\min}$ satisfies $q^2\mid N$; no $q^3$ with $q\neq p$ divides $N$; and for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ on $\bar\rho$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\geq 5$, $r\notin S$, $r\nmid Np$, $p\nmid r-1$, and such that $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\neq (r+1)^2$ for every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $r$ attached to a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $r$. Assume weight-two cusp forms of level $N$ carry an integral structure, and let $\theta_0\colon \mathbb T^S(N,2)\to k$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra generated over $\mathbb Z$ by the $T_\ell$ and $U_q$ outside $S$ such that for all primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell)$ is $X^2-\theta_0(T_\ell)X+\ell$; let $\pi_{T_0}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map from the localisation $\mathrm{heckeLocal}$ of the base-changed Hecke algebra at $\theta_0$ to $\mathcal O$. Finally let $H_0\leq(\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$ be the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/r)^\times$, and assume the operators of the $U_r$-free subfamily commute, that is, the operators $\mathrm{opFamily}$ attached to those generators $g$ of $\mathrm{Gen}(Nr,S)$ for which $g=U_q$ forces $q\mid N$ commute pairwise on $H^1(\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr),\mathcal O)$. Then there are values $c_U\colon \mathrm{Gen}(Nr,S)\to\mathcal O$ and a function $\bar\theta$ on that $U_r$-free subfamily with values in $k$ such that $\bar\theta(T_\ell)=\theta_0(T_\ell)$ for all primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid Nr$, $\bar\theta(U_q)$ is the residue of $c_U(U_q)$ for all primes $q\mid N$, $\bar\theta(\langle d\rangle)=1$ for all $d\in(\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$, and $c_U(U_q)\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ whenever $q\mid N$, $q\neq p$ and $q^2\mid N$; moreover, for the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}H^1(\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr),\mathcal O)$ generated by these operators there exist an idempotent splitting $Sp$ (a complete orthogonal family of idempotents $e_i$ together with the maximal ideals matched to them), an index $i$, and an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_iBe_i$ to $k$ with $\pi_k$ of the corner image of the operator attached to $g$ equal to $\bar\theta(g)$ for every $g$ in the subfamily.
--
--   This is the occurrence statement for the $\Sigma$-refined residual eigensystem: it asserts that the system sending $T_\ell$ to $\theta_0(T_\ell)$, the $U_q$ at primes of raised exponent into the maximal ideal, and the diamond operators to $1$, is realised by a $k$-point of a corner of the $U_r$-free subfamily Hecke algebra acting on the degree-one cohomology of $\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr)$. It feeds the construction of the full corner datum and its pairing in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_fullCorner_pairing_eq_bfam_sigmaResidue_guarded`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_fullCorner_pairing_eq_bfam_sigmaResidue_guarded), the modular side of the rung at $p$.
